The Greens want to close "Luxon's carve-outs" for commercial fishers in the Hauraki Gulf, phase out bottom trawling and protect 30 percent of it by reforming marine protected area legislation.

The carve-outs refer to legislation passed late last year boosting marine protections in the Hauraki Gulf that included a late stage amendment allowing commercial ring-net fishing operators exclusive access to two of high protection areas (HPAs). Most commercial and recreational fishing is prohibited in the HPAs.

